# Everything this repo produces runs on Linux — the OCI node, the containers
# `score` builds, the manifests `conductor` syncs. Force LF line endings so a
# CRLF can never reach a shell script, an Ansible playbook, a systemd unit or a
# container entrypoint and break it with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M".
#
# This matters here specifically because the control machine is Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true. Without this file, git would helpfully convert every
# checked-out script to CRLF and the failure would only show up on the remote
# host, which is the worst place to debug it.
#
# Applies regardless of what core.autocrlf the person cloning has set.
* text=auto eol=lf
